# Cloudflare Pages defaults every static asset to max-age=14400. For four hours after a deploy a
# returning browser therefore keeps its own copy of anything with a stable filename without asking
# the server, which is why a change to app.css or the scoped-style bundle appears to not have
# shipped until the reader empties their cache.
#
# The rule below is the safe default: revalidate. Browsers still keep the file and still get a 304
# when it has not changed, so this costs headers rather than payload. Only paths whose name changes
# with their content are exempted after it. Rules are applied in order and a later rule wins, so
# the exemptions have to follow the default rather than precede it.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Every file the Blazor runtime loads carries a content hash in its name, verified across all 57
# requests the app makes at boot. A new build writes new names, so these can never go stale.
/_framework/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# A sweep's interval series are written once under a sweep id and are never rewritten in place.
/data/sweeps/*/series/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
